Debug.Assert(OLD(index) &lt; _size && index &gt;= 0);
</code>

This assert statement corresponds to the comment "@@@ index passed in is less than the array size and greater than or same as 0" in the given C# code. The line `if (index < 0 || index >= _size) throw new ArgumentOutOfRangeException("nameof(index)", "SR.ArgumentOutOfRange_Index");` is responsible for validating that the index is within the bounds of the array. The `OLD(index)` syntax is used to refer to the value of `index` before the `if` statement is executed. If the assertion condition `(OLD(index) < _size && index >= 0)` is false, the assertion will fail and a Debug.Assert exception will be thrown.
